                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>Snitch or Bewakoof — which is more successful?</h3>
                                        <p>Different metrics. Snitch has higher AOV + faster recent growth. Bewakoof has longer operating history + broader audience + licensed IP moat.</p>
                                        <h3>Can new menswear brands compete with both?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes in category or price-band niching. Rare Rabbit (premium office-wear), The Bear House (heritage-casual), Bombay Shirt Company (custom shirts) all coexist.</p>
                                        <h3>What is the biggest lesson from Snitch's success?</h3>
                                        <p>Positioning discipline (affordable premium) + high content cadence + founder public presence. Combined, powerful.</p>
                                        <h3>What is the biggest lesson from Bewakoof's approach?</h3>
                                        <p>Licensed IP as moat + humour-first content resonance. Different playbook, valid outcomes.</p>
